 "provenance": "Angkor 10 (secret stage, world 0 level 9) secret exit 42,11 from the original spawn, control-only. Start values: weaponTier 1 (plain hammer, obtained in Angkor 4; the Angkor secret stages are reached later in the campaign, so the hammer is the plausible minimum; no hook or ice hammer is needed), maxHealth 4, lives 12, diamonds 99 and redDiamonds 2 as campaign carry-over (they do not matter: the magic diamond lock at 36,11 counts only diamonds collected in this stage, 30 needed). Route: pushes the top stone of the entrance staircase so it cascades to 7,6, lets it roll to 8,7 and pushes it onto plate 9,7 (gate 0), checkpoint 12,7; passes the fire statues during their idle phase; hammers the grass at 9,11 so its stone drops to 9,13, pushes the stones at 7,12 and 5,12 along row 12 so they roll down columns 10 and 11, then pushes the 11,17 stone onto plate 12,17 (gate 1), checkpoint 16,17; descends between the fire statues and stuns the three patrolling green snakes with hammer blows, checkpoint 24,27; slips past the last two snakes; in the grass block hammers 22,16 and 20,16 to drop two stones, pushes 20,18 and then the 19,13 stone (moved over 20,13) so the last one rolls onto plate 24,23 (gate 3); takes the silver key at 27,23, opens the silver lock 31,24 (gate 4), climbs the flame corridor in safe phases, checkpoint 32,12; brings the five movable stones of the upper cave (26,7, 27,3, 25,3 and the grass-released pair at 20,1-20,2) one by one into column 22, where they build a staircase 22,10/23,11/24,12/25,13 and the fifth rolls onto plate 26,15 (gate 5); takes the gold key at 29,15, collects diamonds up to the 30 required by the magic lock, opens the gold lock 35,10 (gate 6) and walks east to the secret exit. No deaths and no damage taken.",
